A REFERENCES added over rows that point nowhere, in a WITHOUT ROWID table:
its rows have no rowid, so the error names the table alone.

== before
CREATE TABLE menu (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, title TEXT NOT NULL) STRICT;
CREATE TABLE course (menu_id INTEGER NOT NULL, name TEXT NOT NULL, PRIMARY KEY (menu_id, name)) STRICT, WITHOUT ROWID;
INSERT INTO menu VALUES (1, 'lunch');
INSERT INTO course VALUES (9, 'roast');

== after
CREATE TABLE menu (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, title TEXT NOT NULL) STRICT;
CREATE TABLE course (menu_id INTEGER NOT NULL REFERENCES menu (id), name TEXT NOT NULL, PRIMARY KEY (menu_id, name)) STRICT, WITHOUT ROWID;

== plan
roux: migrating test.db, 4 steps
  table `course`: aside, to make it anew
    ALTER TABLE "course" RENAME TO "roux_old_course"
  table `course`: as schema.sql makes it
    CREATE TABLE course (menu_id INTEGER NOT NULL REFERENCES menu (id), name TEXT NOT NULL, PRIMARY KEY (menu_id, name)) STRICT, WITHOUT ROWID
  table `course`: its rows, by menu_id, name
    INSERT INTO "course" ("menu_id", "name") SELECT "menu_id", "name" FROM "roux_old_course"
  table `course`: the old one
    DROP TABLE "roux_old_course"

== error
migrating test.db: rows that would break a foreign key: 1; a row of course names no menu
